# Persona template example (#733)

This page is the first persona-rendered document. It is generated from
`docs/templates/persona-template-example.md.in` by
`tools/render_persona_docs.py` with values from `synthetic/personas.json`;
edit the template and re-render, never this file. The design is
`docs/persona-template-design.md`.

In prose, the primary persona is {persona.primary.first_name} {persona.primary.last_name}
(Hebrew form {persona.primary.he_first_name} {persona.primary.he_last_name}, profile
`{persona.primary.profile_id}`, union `{persona.primary.union_id}`), and the spouse
persona is {persona.spouse.first_name} {persona.spouse.last_name}.

The same tokens render identically inside a code fence:

```json
{{"profile": "{persona.primary.profile_id}", "first_name": "{persona.primary.first_name}", "last_name": "{persona.primary.last_name}"}}
```

A literal token is written with doubled braces, so the template syntax itself
reads `{{persona.KEY.FIELD}}`.
